The Company must pay a Termination Fee to Parent when all of the following circumstances are met:
1. The Agreement is terminated under one of these specified scenarios:
   (a) By either the Company or Parent pursuant to Section 8.02(a) (End Date), where Parent has complied with its material obligations (so it is not prohibited from terminating under the section's proviso), the Minimum Condition is unsatisfied, and all required Offer Conditions (No Legal Prohibition, Antitrust Approvals, FIRB Approval, New Zealand Overseas Investment Regime) are satisfied;
   (b) By either the Company or Parent pursuant to Section 8.02(c) (Termination of Offer), with the same Parent compliance, Minimum Condition status, and Offer Conditions satisfaction as above;
   (c) By Parent pursuant to Section 8.04(a) (Company Breach).
2. At the time of termination, a bona fide Acquisition Proposal has been publicly disclosed, or a person has publicly announced an intention to make one (and this proposal/intention has not been publicly withdrawn prior to termination).
3. Within 12 months of termination, one of the following occurs:
   (a) The Company or its subsidiaries enter into a definitive Alternative Acquisition Agreement and the related Acquisition Proposal is consummated;
   (b) The Company Board approves or recommends an Acquisition Proposal to stockholders and that proposal is consummated;
   (c) An Acquisition Proposal (with a 50% ownership threshold replacing the standard 15%) is consummated.
The fee is due via wire transfer of immediately available funds upon the consummation of the applicable Acquisition Proposal.

Company Acquisition Transactions (excluding the Merger) include the following types, with a 25% threshold applying to specific categories:
1. Mergers, consolidations, amalgamations, share exchanges, business combinations, joint ventures, reorganizations, or similar transactions involving the Company;
2. Transactions where either (i) any person or group acquires beneficial or record ownership of securities (or instruments convertible into/exercisable for/exchangeable for such securities) representing 25% or more of the Company's outstanding voting power, or (ii) the Company or its subsidiaries issue such securities representing 25% or more of the Company's outstanding voting power (after giving effect to the transaction);
3. Sales, exchanges, transfers, acquisitions, or dispositions of either (i) 25% or more of the consolidated assets of the Company and its subsidiaries (including equity securities of subsidiaries), or (ii) any business(es) or their assets that account for 25% or more of the Company and its subsidiaries' consolidated net revenues or net income;
4. Tender or exchange offers that, if consummated, would result in any person or group acquiring beneficial or record ownership of securities (or convertible/exercisable/exchangeable instruments) representing 25% or more of the Company's outstanding voting power.

Inphi Corporation would be required to pay Marvell Technology Group Ltd. a $300,000,000 Company Termination Fee under two distinct combined sets of circumstances:

1. First scenario (per Section 8.3(c)):
   - The agreement is terminated by either party pursuant to Section 8.1(b);
   - At or before termination, a Company Acquisition Proposal was made known to Inphi or publicly disclosed, announced, commenced, submitted, or made;
   - Prior to termination, Inphi’s stockholders had not taken a final vote on adopting the agreement;
   - Within 12 months of termination, a Company Acquisition Transaction (with a modified definition where references to "15%" are deemed "50%", and it includes mergers/business combinations where Inphi’s pre-transaction stockholders retain or acquire at least 40% ownership of the relevant entity’s shares/equity) is consummated, or a definitive agreement for such a transaction is executed.

2. Second scenario (per Section 8.3(d)):
   - The agreement is terminated by either party pursuant to Section 8.1(d);
   - At or before termination, a Company Acquisition Proposal was publicly disclosed, announced, or commenced and was not withdrawn at least 10 Business Days prior to the Inphi Stockholders’ Meeting;
   - Within 12 months of termination, a Company Acquisition Transaction (with the same modified definition as above) is consummated, or a definitive agreement for such a transaction is executed.
